# case: 730-native-clients-run
# what: the Dockerfile layer that RESTORES the build toolchain never fires -- its
#       condition is changed to a value KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN can never hold, so
#       build-essential/libyaml-dev/zlib1g-dev/libssl-dev stay stripped even though
#       build.sh correctly passed KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=1. This is the state that
#       shipped before that layer existed, and the reason it was added.
#
#       This targets 730's `gcc` assertion specifically, which until now had NO
#       demonstration: 730-db-clients-not-space-split (the patch formerly misnamed
#       730-toolchain-stripped) removes psql/mysql/mongosh and leaves gcc untouched,
#       so the header's stated reason for asserting gcc -- "if the Dockerfile ever
#       stripped the toolchain again despite the flag" -- was an unbacked claim
#       sitting next to a patch whose NAME implied it was backed.
#
#       Mutating the Dockerfile rather than build.sh is deliberate. build.sh sets
#       KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=1 whenever ruby OR db-clients is set, and the native
#       variant sets both, so no build.sh edit can produce KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=0
#       there. Forcing the ARG to 0 directly is also not it: Dockerfile:331 fails
#       the build outright on RUBY_RUNTIME=1 with KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN!=1, so the
#       image would never build and 730 would fail as "image did not build" -- a
#       named failure, but not this one. Defeating the restore layer while leaving
#       the flag truthful reproduces the actual defect: the flag says keep, the
#       image does not have it.
#
#       MUST BE DEMONSTRATED ALONE (--cases 730-native-clients-run). rvm compiles
#       Ruby from source at container start and needs gcc, so 740/750/760 would
#       fail for this mutation's reason before reaching their own assertions --
#       the masking that cost three extra dispatches last increment.
#
#       Expected: 730's gcc assertion FAILS ("gcc is on PATH"), while psql, mysql,
#       mongosh, convert and wkhtmltopdf all still PASS -- they are ordinary apt
#       packages installed by other layers and are untouched by this.
#
diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
index ee36aec..6c1ffe6 100644
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -288,7 +288,7 @@ RUN if [ -n "$DB_CLIENTS" ]; then \
 # DB driver gems, and Python source wheels compile at runtime, so put a minimal
 # toolchain back when KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=1 (set by build.sh for ruby OR db-clients).
 ARG KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=0
-RUN if [ "$KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN" = "1" ]; then \
+RUN if [ "$KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN" = "NEVER" ]; then \
       apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
         build-essential libyaml-dev zlib1g-dev libssl-dev && \
       rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*; \
